course: dictionary
lesson: 7277
title: One word, three meanings: pine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning is meant. Pine can name a tree, a pale wood, or a feeling of missing someone very much.
explain: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» Here pine cones are things you can pick up, so pine means the tree that makes them. Pine is a noun here, a name for a thing.
explain: Pine can also be a verb, an action word. «The lonely puppy pines for its owner» means the puppy misses its owner very much and feels sad. Check it: swap in your meaning, "the puppy misses its owner very much and feels sad", and it still makes sense.
fact: A pine is a tall evergreen tree with thin, sharp leaves called needles.
fact: Pine needles stay green all year, and pine trees make seeds inside pine cones.
fact: Pine is also the pale wood of this tree, used for furniture.
fact: Rosin is hardened pine resin, rubbed on a bow so the hair grips the strings.
fact: As a verb, pine means to miss someone or something very much and feel sad.
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» Pine cones grow on which kind of plant? | *Pine trees | Maple trees | Rose bushes | Oak trees
exercise: «The pine trees nearest the reactor were killed by radiation and turned red-brown.» What does pine mean here? | A sharp, thin leaf | To miss someone very much | A pale wood used for furniture | *A tall evergreen tree with needles
exercise: Ami says, «I pine for my gran when I am at camp.» What does pine mean? | To climb very high | To paint a wall pale | To cut down a tree | *To miss someone very much and feel sad
test: «Rosin is hardened pine resin, rubbed on a bow.» What does rosin come from? | Oak trees | *Pine trees | Horses | Bows
test: «The taiga is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.» In this sentence, what kind of thing is pine? | A kind of cloud | A kind of bird | *A kind of tree | A kind of stone
exam: Pine can be a noun or a verb. Which sentence uses pine as a verb? | The pine furniture was pale and light. | The pine trees made the forest smell fresh. | *The lonely puppy pined for its family. | Pine cones fell onto the path.
